course: dictionary
lesson: 10287
title: Tortoise: a slow animal with a shell
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tortoise is a slow animal that lives on land. It has a hard, high shell on its back. When it is scared, it can pull its head and legs inside the shell to keep safe. «Pet tortoises often live 50 years» tells you that a tortoise can live a very long time.
explain: Tortoises are reptiles, and they eat plants. A turtle is similar, but it lives mostly in water, while a tortoise lives on land. Clues in a sentence help you work out meaning: «a hard, high shell» tells you what a tortoise looks like.
explain: The shell is part of the tortoise's skeleton, joined to its ribs and backbone, so a tortoise can never leave its shell. Context clues often explain the word for you, so read the words around the one you don't know.
fact: A tortoise is a slow animal with a hard, high shell that lives on land.
fact: A tortoise can pull its head and legs inside its shell to stay safe.
fact: Tortoises can live a very long time, some more than 100 years.
fact: Jonathan, a giant tortoise on St Helena, is reported to be around 190 years old.
fact: Tortoises are reptiles, and they eat plants.
exercise: What is a tortoise? | *A slow animal with a hard, high shell that lives on land | A fish that swims in the sea | A plant with thick green leaves | A fast bird that lives in trees
exercise: «Galápagos giant tortoises ... on dry islands their saddle-shaped shells let them stretch up to tall cactus.» Why can they reach up to tall cactus? | *Their saddle-shaped shells let them stretch up | They climb trees with sharp claws | They can fly up to the top
exercise: A tortoise walks 3 metres every minute. How far does it walk in 4 minutes? Use distance = speed × time. | 1 metre | 7 metres | 34 metres | *12 metres
test: A tortoise pulls its head inside its shell. Why might it do this? | It wants to fly away | It is trying to catch a fish | *To keep safe from danger
test: In the story «The Tortoise and the Hare», which animal wins the race? | The hare, because it is the fastest | Neither, because the race is cancelled | Both at the same time | *The tortoise, because slow and steady wins
exam: Which animal lives mostly in water? | A cactus | *A turtle | A tortoise | A hare
